PathfinderNavigation
====================

Control script for Pathfinder mod navigation. Handles pathfinding commands and triggers callbacks to linked programmable blocks.

Requirements
------------
- Functional `IMyRemoteControl` on the same grid
- Pathfinder mod installed

Setup
-----
1. Load script into a programmable block.
2. Name the block with `[PF]` if you want other scripts to find it automatically.
3. Script automatically finds and uses the remote control on the same grid.

API
---
Commands (run in PB terminal):
- `start` – Begin pathfinding to current destination (set via Pathfinder mod terminal)
- `start GPS:Name:X:Y:Z:` – Start pathfinding to GPS coordinates
- `start GPSName` – Start pathfinding to GPS name (searches GPS list and beacons)
- `start GPSName|PBName` – Start pathfinding and link callback PB (pipe separator)
- `start GPS:Name:X:Y:Z:|PBName` – Start with coordinates and link callback PB
- `stop` – Stop pathfinding

Callbacks (sent to linked programmable block):
- `pf_start` – Pathfinding started
- `pf_stop` – Pathfinding stopped
- `pf_nopath` – No path found

Notes
-----
- Destination can be set via Pathfinder mod terminal properties or command arguments
- GPS names match beacons by grid name (e.g., "MyGrid" matches "MyGrid - BeaconName")
- Use pipe `|` to link a programmable block for callbacks
- Callback PB name is matched case-insensitively
